VALUES (4400093533030135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Data Structure in Data Structure. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include one verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Introduction to Queue in Data Structure. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include one verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Introduction to Sorting in Data Structure. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include one verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Introduction to Hashing in Data Structure. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include one verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Data Structure is covered in the syllabus unit “Introduction to Basics of Data Structure”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Data Representation, Data Types: Primitive and Non-Primitive, Algorithm, Time Complexity, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Data Representation; Data Types: Primitive and Non-Primitive; Algorithm; Time Complexity. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Data Structure task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A queue normally uses first-in, first-out ordering. Enqueue adds at the rear and dequeue removes from the front; this is useful for scheduling and buffering.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Queue Operations: Insertion; Deletion; Types of Queue: Simple; Circular. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Data Structure task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Sorting is covered in the syllabus unit “Sorting & Searching Techniques”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Types of Sorting : Bubble Sort, Insertion Sort, Selection Sort, Merge Sort, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Types of Sorting : Bubble Sort; Insertion Sort; Selection Sort; Merge Sort. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Data Structure task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Hashing maps a key to a table location. Collisions can be handled with methods such as chaining or open addressing.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Hash Table; Various Hash function : Division Method; Multiplication & Mid-square Method; Applications of Hashing. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Data Structure task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

