VALUES (4400093533010125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Concept of Object-Oriented Programming in the context of Introduction to Object Oriented Concepts. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to C++ programming in the context of Programming Basics. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to Class in the context of Classes, Objects and Functions. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Define Constructor in the context of Constructor and Destructor. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concept of Object-Oriented Programming is covered in the syllabus unit “Introduction to Object Oriented Concepts”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Applications of Object- Oriented Programming, Characteristics of Object-Oriented Programming, Object-Oriented Programming vs Procedure Programming, Pros of OOP, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Applications of Object- Oriented Programming; Characteristics of Object-Oriented Programming; Object-Oriented Programming vs Procedure Programming; Pros of OOP. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to C++ programming is covered in the syllabus unit “Programming Basics”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Basic structure of C++, Namespace, Directives, Using I/O Operators, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Basic structure of C++; Namespace; Directives; Using I/O Operators. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Class is covered in the syllabus unit “Classes, Objects and Functions”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Scope of class and accessing members of class, Class Object, Function Prototype, Function Calling, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Scope of class and accessing members of class; Class Object; Function Prototype; Function Calling. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A C++ constructor initializes an object, shares the class name and has no return type; overloads can provide different initialization paths.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Types of Constructors: Default constructor; Parameterized constructor; Copy constructor; Dynamic Constructor Destructor. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

