xpected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Class is covered in the syllabus unit “Classes, Objects and Functions”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Scope of class and accessing members of class, Class Object, Function Prototype, Function Calling, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Scope of class and accessing members of class; Class Object; Function Prototype; Function Calling. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A C++ constructor initializes an object, shares the class name and has no return type; overloads can provide different initialization paths.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Types of Constructors: Default constructor; Parameterized constructor; Copy constructor; Dynamic Constructor Destructor. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concept of objects and pointers is covered in the syllabus unit “Virtual Functions and polymorphism”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to this pointer, Virtual Functions, Pure Virtual Functions, Types of Polymorphism, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as this pointer; Virtual Functions; Pure Virtual Functions; Types of Polymorphism. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Object Oriented Programming With C++ task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

